Set out a rational straight line {DI}. Apply {DE|DEh}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}, to {DI} producing {DG} as breadth. Apply {DH|DHh}, equal to twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}, to {DI} producing {DF} as breadth. Then the remainder {FE|FEh} equals the square on {AC}. [!just II.7]

Now, since the squares on {AB} and {BC} are medial and commensurable, therefore {DE|DEh} is also medial. [!just X.15, X.23.Cor]

And it is applied to the rational straight line {DI}, producing {DG} as breadth, therefore {DG} is rational and incommensurable in length with {DI}. [!just X.22]

Again, since the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is medial, therefore twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also medial. [!just X.23.Cor]

And it equals {DH|DHh}, therefore {DH|DHh} is also medial.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {DI}, producing {DF} as breadth, therefore {DF} is rational and incommensurable in length with {DI}. [!just X.22]

Since {AB} and {BC} are commensurable in square only, therefore {AB} is incommensurable in length with {BC}. Therefore the square on {AB} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BC}. [!just X.11]

But the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC} is commensurable with the square on {AB}, and twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is commensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BC}, therefore twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is incommensurable with the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}. [!just X.15, X.6; X.13]

But {DE|DEh} equals the sum of the squares on {AB} and {BC}, and {DH|DHh} equals twice the rectangle {AB} by {BC}, therefore {DE|DEh} is incommensurable with {DH|DHh}. But {DE|DEh} is to {DH|DHh} as {GD|DG} is to {DF}, therefore {GD|DG} is incommensurable with {DF}. [!just VI.1; X.11]

And both are rational, therefore {GD|DG} and {DF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {FG} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

But {DI} is rational, and the rectangle contained by a rational and an irrational straight line is irrational, and its side is irrational. [!just X.20]

And {AC} is the side of {FE|FEh}, therefore {AC} is irrational.

Let it be called a second apotome of a medial straight line.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
